\n\nTraditional music: The original meaning of the term \"folk music\" was synonymous with the term \"Traditional music\", also often including Roots music; the term \"Traditional music\" was given its more specific meaning to distinguish it from the other definitions that \"Folk music\" is now considered to encompass.\nFolk music can also describe a particular kind of popular music which is based on traditional music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Olivia Rodrigo", "streams": 13623, "best_position": 80}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": 12874, "best_position": 91}, {"artist": "Alex G", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Clairo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Phoebe Bridgers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sufjan Stevens", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "grunge": {"genre": "grunge", "country_code": "no", "country_name": "Norway", "summary": "Grunge is a subgenre of rock music that emerged during the mid-1980s in the American state of Washington, almost entirely in the Seattle area. \"Grunge\" was initially used to describe only the emerging music scene in Seattle; an unkempt collective of bands each with their own scuzzy take on 70s rock that was a reaction against the technicality and pretension of contemporary and dominant metal. Inspired by hardcore punk, metal (particularly 70s heavy metal like Sabbath and Led Zep and the overdriven proto-punk of the Stooges), and early alt.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Foo Fighters", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Muse", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Radiohead", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smashing Pumpkins", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "no", "country_name": "Norway", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Karpe", "streams": 90313, "best_position": 19}, {"artist": "Zara Larsson", "streams": 34873, "best_position": 39}, {"artist": "Mac Miller", "streams": 21445, "best_position": 35}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": 17418, "best_position": 49}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": 17241, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "metal": {"genre": "metal", "country_code": "no", "country_name": "Norway", "summary": "A metal is a material that exhibits a lustrous appearance when polished or fractured and conducts electricity and heat relatively efficiently. These properties are associated with the presence of electrons at the Fermi level. Metals are typically ductile, allowing them to be drawn into wires, and malleable, enabling them to be shaped by hammering or pressing.\n\nA metal may be a chemical element, such as iron, an alloy such as stainless steel, or a molecular compound such as polymeric sulfur nitride.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Black Sabbath", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Metallica", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Nirvana", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Red Hot Chili Peppers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "nu metal": {"genre": "nu metal", "country_code": "no", "country_name": "Norway", "summary": "Nu metal is a subgenre of alternative metal that blends elements of heavy metal with influences from other genres such as hip hop, funk, industrial, and grunge. It typically emphasises rhythm and syncopation, with guitar work often involving down-tuned seven-string guitars to create a heavier sound. Guitar solos and technical displays are generally less common in nu metal. Vocal styles vary and may include singing, rapping, screaming, and occasionally growling.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Deftones", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Linkin Park", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Slipknot", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "System of a Down", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "no", "country_name": "Norway", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenre